IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-nouns`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-art37-43-final`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art32-36-appeals`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-nouns`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-vintage`
IMPORT `int-wiring`

-- int-h-appeal.l4: headline (f) of the integration layer: who may appeal to the Charity Tribunal against which decision, and by when?
-- Article 33 (group G8) lists the decisions of the Commissioner that may be appealed and by whom. Its third-party appeal (33(5)) needs two facts at TWO times -- the application and the appeal --
-- that other groups decide: that the entity met the charity test (group G2, IP8, evaluated on the facts at each time: IP9) and that the name is undesirable (group G4, Article 12(1), IP18 at each time).
-- The decision appealed is a decision of the Commissioner (IP27) that the deciding group produced (for an application: group G4, `Art 11 what the Commissioner must do on the application`).
-- "By when" is Article 36(2)(a): a time limit an Order sets, running from the notice of the decision (Article 36(2)(b)), and the date of the notice is fixed by Article 38 (group G7, IP34).
-- No Order under Article 36(2) is among the sources: a case with no limit supplied is not answered as "in time" or "out of time" (it refuses, as group G8 does), so the answer to "who" and the answer to "by when" are separate exports.
-- It rests on Articles 5, 12, 32, 33, 35, 36 and 38 and refuses for a day before Part 8 (other than Article 32) was in force (1 May 2018) and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (f): who may appeal, against which decision, and by when?`

DECLARE `Appeal case` HAS
    appeal IS AN `Appeal under Article 33` @desc The appellant, the decision of the Commissioner appealed, and whether the decision concerns the appellant's own application or registration
    body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The entity the decision is about (the applicant or the charity)
    `charity test facts at the time of the application` IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The facts the charity test reads as they stood at the time of the application (Article 33(5)(a))
    `charity test facts at the time of the appeal` IS A `Facts for the charity test in the case` @desc The facts the charity test reads as they stand at the time of the appeal
    `opinion on the name at the time of the application` IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The Commissioner's opinion on the name at the time of the application (Article 33(5)(b))
    `opinion on the name at the time of the appeal` IS AN `Opinion of the Commissioner on a name` @desc The opinion at the time of the appeal
    `day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day of the decision appealed
    notice IS A MAYBE `Notice of a decision in the case` @desc The notice of the decision, if one was given
    `day the appeal was lodged` IS A DATE @desc The day on which the appeal was lodged
    limit IS A MAYBE `Time limit prescribed under Article 36(2)(a)` @desc The time limit an Order under Article 36(2)(a) prescribes; NOTHING if no Order is supplied (none is among the sources)

DECLARE `Answer on who may appeal` HAS
    `the right of appeal` IS A `Right of appeal under Article 33` @desc Group G8: Article 33: which paragraph gives the right, or that Part 8 gives none
    `the person may appeal the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G8: Article 33
    `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9, group G2
    `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP9, group G2
    `the name is undesirable at the time of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18 at the first time, group G4
    `the name is undesirable at the time of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc IP18 at the second time, group G4
    `the date on which the notice of the decision is served` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc IP34, group G7: Article 38; NOTHING if no notice was given
    `the last day to bring the appeal` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc Group G8: Article 36(2)(a); NOTHING if no Order prescribes a limit of days (none is among the sources)

-- The date of the notice of the decision, if one was given, fixed by group G7 (Article 38).
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      notice IS A MAYBE `Notice of a decision in the case` @desc The notice of the decision, if any
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Int IP34 the date on which the notice of the decision was served` readings notice MEANS
    CONSIDER notice
      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
      WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`Int IP34 the date on which the notice of a decision was served` readings n)

-- The dates Article 36(2) reads.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      case IS AN `Appeal case` @desc The case
GIVETH A `Dates of an appeal under Article 36(2)`
`Int the dates of the appeal` readings case MEANS
    `Dates of an appeal under Article 36(2)` WITH
        `day of the decision` IS case's `day of the decision`
        `day of the notice of the decision` IS `Int IP34 the date on which the notice of the decision was served` readings (case's notice)
        `day the appeal was lodged` IS case's `day the appeal was lodged`

GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      case IS AN `Appeal case` @desc The case
GIVETH AN `Answer on who may appeal`
`Int (f) the answer on who may appeal under the text` readings day vintage case MEANS
    `Answer on who may appeal` WITH
        `the right of appeal` IS `Art 33 the right of appeal` g8 (case's appeal) metThen meetsNow undesirableThen undesirableNow
        `the person may appeal the decision` IS `Art 33 the person may appeal the decision` g8 (case's appeal) metThen meetsNow undesirableThen undesirableNow
        `the entity met the charity test at the time of the application` IS metThen
        `the entity meets the charity test at the time of the appeal` IS meetsNow
        `the name is undesirable at the time of the application` IS undesirableThen
        `the name is undesirable at the time of the appeal` IS undesirableNow
        `the date on which the notice of the decision is served` IS `Int IP34 the date on which the notice of the decision was served` readings (case's notice)
        `the last day to bring the appeal` IS
            CONSIDER case's limit
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST prescribed THEN
                CONSIDER prescribed
                  WHEN `no Order has prescribed a time limit` THEN NOTHING
                  WHEN `an Order prescribes a time limit of days` n THEN JUST (`Art 36(2) the last day to bring the appeal` g8 (`Int the dates of the appeal` readings case) n)
    WHERE
        g8 MEANS readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`
        entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage EMPTY day (case's body)
        metThen MEANS `Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity ((case's body)'s purposes) (case's `charity test facts at the time of the application`)
        meetsNow MEANS `Int IP8 the entity meets the charity test` readings vintage entity ((case's body)'s purposes) (case's `charity test facts at the time of the appeal`)
        undesirableThen MEANS `Int IP18 the name is undesirable` readings (case's `opinion on the name at the time of the application`)
        undesirableNow MEANS `Int IP18 the name is undesirable` readings (case's `opinion on the name at the time of the appeal`)

`Int (f) the units the question rests on` MEANS
    LIST `Int Article` 5, `Int Article` 12, `Int Article` 32, `Int Article` 33, `Int Article` 36, `Int Article` 38

@export Who may appeal to the Charity Tribunal against which decision of the Commissioner (Article 33): an applicant against a refusal to register or to enter in the restricted section, a registered charity against five named decisions, a person served with a notice against its requirement, the Attorney General against any decision, and any other person against a decision to register where the entity did not meet the charity test and the name was undesirable at both the time of the application and the time of the appeal; with the date on which the notice of the decision is served (Article 38) and the last day to bring the appeal where an Order sets a time limit (Article 36(2)). Refuses for a day before Part 8 (other than Article 32) was in force (1 May 2018), and for a day on which the text of the Law changed and the two texts answer differently
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
      case IS AN `Appeal case` @desc The appellant, the decision appealed, the facts at the two times, the notice of the decision and the time limit
GIVETH AN `Answer on who may appeal`
`Int (f) who may appeal the decision` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (f) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            (GIVEN vintage YIELD `Int (f) the answer on who may appeal under the text` readings day vintage case))

@export Whether an appeal to the Charity Tribunal was brought in time (Article 36(2)): within the time limit an Order under Article 36(2)(a) prescribes, counted from the notice of the decision whose date is fixed by Article 38. It refuses when no Order is supplied (none is among the sources), as it does for a day before Part 8 (other than Article 32) was in force
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the question is asked
      case IS AN `Appeal case` @desc The case
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int (f) was the appeal brought in time` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` `Int (f) the units the question rests on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Art 36(2) the appeal is in time` (readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) (`Int the dates of the appeal` readings case) (case's limit))
